<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kwantung Army</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kwantung Army was a group of the Imperial Japanese Army stationed in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from the early twentieth century. Its officers staged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukden-incident">Mukden Incident</a> of 1931, which led to the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, and often acted independently of the government in Tokyo. Its insubordination illustrates the military's growing control over policy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> before its defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kwantung-army.jpg" alt="Kwantung Army" width="320" height="124" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kwantung_Army_Headquarters.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
